  "notes": "An ichidan verb with two distinct uses: as a main verb meaning \"to obtain\" and as an auxiliary indicating possibility.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- No standard intransitive pair\n- Pattern: [noun]⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{得|え}る\n\nAS MAIN VERB (to obtain/gain):\n- ⟦{許可|きょか}→許可：00259_kyoka⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{得|え}る: to obtain permission\n- ⟦{信頼|しんらい}→信頼：03268_shinrai⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{得|え}る: to gain trust\n- ⟦{知識|ちしき}→知識：01463_chishiki⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{得|え}る: to acquire knowledge\n- More formal/literary than ⟦{手|て}→手：00569_te⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦{入|い}れる→入れる：01098_ireru⟧ or ⟦もらう→もらう：00520_morau⟧\n\nAS AUXILIARY (〜{得|え}る = can/possible):\nAttached to the masu-stem of verbs:\n- ⟦あり→ある：00006_aru⟧{得|え}る: possible / ⟦あり→ある：00006_aru⟧{得|え}ない: impossible\n- ⟦{起|お}こり→起こる：01910_okoru⟧{得|え}る: can happen\n- ⟦{考|かんが}え→考える：00856_kangaeru⟧{得|え}る⟦{限|かぎ}り→限り：00133_kagiri⟧: to the extent imaginable\n\nALTERNATIVE READING:\n{得|う}る is a classical/literary variant. The negative ⟦あり→ある：00006_aru⟧{得|え}ない is far more common than ⟦あり→ある：00006_aru⟧{得|う}ない in modern speech.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n- {得|え}ている: has obtained / currently possesses (resultative state)\n- Note: {得|え}る is punctual (the moment of obtaining), so {得|え}ている describes the resulting state of having something, not an ongoing acquisition. For example, ⟦{信頼|しんらい}→信頼：03268_shinrai⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{得|え}ている means \"enjoys/has trust,\" not \"is in the process of earning trust.\"",
